{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrzoj3xEvHNSTghR4Nx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Line.is_parallel`, `is_perpendicular`, `angle_between` and `smallest_angle_between` now raise `TypeError` when either argument isn't a `LinearEntity`. The existing tests in `tests/test_line.py` pass (36 passed). I didn't run your `Line.is_parallel(Line(Point(0,0), Point(1,1)), Point(0,0))` example directly, and I added no test for the new behavior.\n\nThe cause was the type check in all four methods. It used `and`, so it only raised when *both* arguments were invalid. A valid line paired with a `Point` got past it and crashed on `.direction`. I changed `and` to `or` in each check in `sympy/geometry/line.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":19440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289},"output_tokens":239,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ad91da2-e571-4b84-aabd-ab46d11e9389","uuid":"bab6fa5c-c034-4293-a27a-183bb6c0b251","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:11:18.388Z","request_id":"req_011ChLrzoQhJCwHvaWQ3vDDP"}
